2. TECHNOLOGY STACK
==================================================

Frontend:
- React.
- TypeScript.
- Vite-compatible project structure.
- Tailwind CSS.
- shadcn/ui or equivalent accessible components.
- Lucide icons.

Application:
- Installable Progressive Web App.
- Service worker.
- Web App Manifest.
- Offline application shell.
- Responsive mobile, tablet, and desktop UI.

Local persistence:
- IndexedDB.
- Dexie.js for structured local data.
- OPFS for local file storage when supported.
- IndexedDB Blob storage fallback.
- Versioned database migrations.

Documents:
- PDF.js for PDF rendering and text extraction.
- Tesseract.js for local OCR.
- Web Workers for heavy processing.
- File hashing using Web Crypto.

Security:
- Web Crypto API.
- AES-GCM encryption.
- Password-derived key wrapping.
- Vetted password KDF implementation.
- No plaintext password storage.
- No exposed API keys.
- Explicit lock and unlock flow.

AI:
- Gemini API through server-side integration only.
- Use a supported current Gemini model.
- Keep the integration behind an AI service abstraction.
- Never put Gemini API keys in client-side code.
- Use server-side secrets in AI Studio.
- If Gemini is not configured, show an informative unavailable state.

Do not use Firebase, Firestore, Firebase Storage, or cloud authentication for the offline core.

Avoid unnecessary external dependencies.

