8. DOCUMENT PROCESSING AND OCR
==================================================

Create a real local processing pipeline.

For each uploaded document:

1. Validate its file signature and MIME type.
2. Calculate a file hash.
3. Detect duplicates.
4. Save the document locally.
5. Extract selectable PDF text using PDF.js.
6. If text is insufficient, run local OCR.
7. Run rule-based document classification.
8. Extract candidate metadata.
9. Store extracted text locally.
10. Show the user a review screen.
11. Allow editing and confirmation.
12. Update search index and timeline.

Use Tesseract.js locally.

Use Web Workers for OCR and other heavy processing.

Never block the main UI thread during large document processing.

Show:
- Queued.
- Processing.
- OCR in progress.
- Extracting.
- Review required.
- Completed.
- Failed.

Provide retry and cancel actions.

For every extracted field, record:
- Field name.
- Extracted value.
- Confidence when available.
- Source page or location when available.
- Verification status.
- Creation timestamp.

AI-extracted fields must default to unverified.

Never mark extracted values as verified automatically.

